    "a number of findings cited here apply to nature broadly, rather than specifically to indoor vegetation, and should therefore be taken as suggestive rather than conclusive.",
    "research has been limited, however, to sealed and controlled chambers, where the plant density per volume is much higher than it is in the real world, it is challenging to extrapolate from the data.",
    "most of the information discussed in the reviewed literature (Table 3) is mostly self-reported (e.g. questionnaires, interviews, surveys) and it is important to note the implications of potential response bias.",
    "it may be difficult to create a controlled outdoor environment that could be compared to biophilic indoor settings.",
    "More testing needs to be undertaken in the field, with a particular emphasis on the capacity of plants to reduce energy consumption in the room scale.",
